-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I32: I29's topology with the difference between the two
-- schemes moved ENTIRELY into the constraint set.  Every other importer cell in this
-- corpus differs in the body of the type, so none of them can see a comparison that
-- descends into the body and skips the constraints.
--
-- `Eq a => b -> a -> String` and `Debug a => t -> a -> String` are not
-- alpha-equivalent by any reading, so S2-IMPORT-DIFFER requires the warning.  The
-- resolution is I29's and is not what the cell is about: `Taggable` is nameable by
-- its type name, `Box` carries a live impl, so the occurrence dispatches to the
-- method and prints `iface`, never `prov`.
import ifc.{Taggable, Box(..)}
import prov.{tagOf}

main = println (tagOf (Box 3) 9)
